E VariationSubject                              | Api/TilingSpecification.h        | 98-104    | How cells differ from one another, if at all — `54` §1's three rows. third row is the one most likely to be implemented as noise and is the one that must not be: a permutation of the cell ordinal is reproducible, and sampled noise makes the same document reopen looking different.
